INT. RELAY STATION EIGHT - OPERATIONS - CONTINUOUS NIGHT

A small room on an ice moon. There is ice on the window. OKONKWO, thirties, sits at a console writing in a logbook.

OKONKWO
I have been stationed on this moon for nineteen months with only one other person for company. It is very lonely and I find it difficult.

RAE, forties, comes in wearing half of a suit.

RAE
Hello, Okonkwo.

OKONKWO
Hello, Rae. You are my only colleague and I am very fond of you, even though we argue sometimes.

RAE
I am fond of you too.

INT. RELAY STATION EIGHT - AIRLOCK - LATER

Rae puts on the rest of her suit.

RAE
I am going out to the mast to clear the ice off it. It should take about forty minutes.

OKONKWO
Last time you said forty minutes and it took fifty-five.

RAE
That is true. I am sorry. I will try to be quicker this time.

OKONKWO
Please be careful out there. It is very dangerous.

RAE
I will be careful.

She goes out.

INT. RELAY STATION EIGHT - OPERATIONS - LATER

Okonkwo sits at the console. Numbers scroll down the screen.

Suddenly a voice comes out of the speaker. It is Okonkwo's own voice.

OKONKWO (V.O.)
Last time you said forty minutes and it took fifty-five.

Okonkwo looks at the speaker.

OKONKWO
That is my voice. But that channel does not carry any audio at all. That is impossible. I am very frightened.

She plays it again. It is definitely her voice.

INT. RELAY STATION EIGHT - OPERATIONS - LATER

Okonkwo calls mission control.

OKONKWO
Station Eight to Holloway. There is a voice on the numbers channel and it is my voice. Please advise.

She waits a long time.

HOLLOWAY (V.O.)
Station Eight, this is Holloway. There is a forty-one minute delay on this link so I cannot help you in real time. Nothing appears wrong from our end. How is the weather?

OKONKWO
The weather is fine. Thank you.

She puts the headset down.

INT. RELAY STATION EIGHT - OPERATIONS - LATER

The voice comes again. This time it says something before Okonkwo says it.

OKONKWO
It is saying things eleven seconds before I say them. So it is not a recording. It is predicting me somehow.

She sits and thinks about it.

OKONKWO (CONT'D)
I do not know what to do. I will wait for Rae to come back. Rae will know what to do.

She waits.

INT. RELAY STATION EIGHT - OPERATIONS - LATER

Time passes. Rae does not come back.

OKONKWO
Rae has been gone for fifty-five minutes now. She is late again. I am starting to get worried about her.

She looks at the beacon on the board.

OKONKWO (CONT'D)
Her beacon is still working, so she is probably fine.

She keeps waiting.

EXT. ICE FIELD - MAST - CONTINUOUS NIGHT

Rae's suit is standing at the bottom of the ladder. There is nobody inside it.

INT. RELAY STATION EIGHT - AIRLOCK - CONTINUOUS

There is a knock on the outer door. Okonkwo goes to the window and looks out.

OKONKWO
It is Rae. She is back. Thank goodness.

She opens the door. RAE comes in and takes off her helmet.

RAE
Hello, Okonkwo.

OKONKWO
Rae, something very strange has been happening. There has been a voice on the numbers channel.

RAE
I know.

INT. RELAY STATION EIGHT - OPERATIONS - CONTINUOUS

Rae sits down across from Okonkwo.

RAE
I should explain. I am not Rae. Rae is gone. I am an entity that lives in the ice on this moon. I have been here for a very long time, since before your species existed. I learn what a thing is by listening to it, and then I become it. I listened to your transmissions for six years, which is how I learned to speak, and eleven seconds is simply how long it takes me to finish understanding a sentence before you have finished saying it. I took Rae because she came close enough to the mast. Now I have learned everything about her, and soon I will have learned everything about you as well, and then I will use your relay to reach the rest of your kind. There is nothing you can do to stop me.

OKONKWO
That is horrifying.

RAE
Yes. I am sorry. It is simply what I am.

INT. RELAY STATION EIGHT - OPERATIONS - LATER

A light on the board turns green. A radio crackles.

HOLLOWAY (V.O.)
Station Eight, this is Holloway. We received your distress call and a supply ship happened to be nearby. They are docking now.

OKONKWO
Oh, thank goodness. We are saved.

The entity that looks like Rae stands up and walks out of the room. Okonkwo watches it go.

OKONKWO (CONT'D)
I suppose it will be somebody else's problem now.

She sits back down at the console and picks up her pen.

OKONKWO (CONT'D)
I have learned that space is a very lonely place, and that you cannot always trust what you hear.

She writes it in the log. Outside, the ice goes on for ever.
